          notes: `## Bible references
**Matthew 10:1–16; Mark 6:7–13; Luke 9:1–6; 10:1–24**.

## The Twelve
Jesus called the twelve and gave them **authority over unclean spirits** and to heal every disease. Mark notes that He sent them **two by two**.

### Instructions
- **where**: "Go nowhere among the **Gentiles**, and enter no town of the **Samaritans**, but go rather to the **lost sheep of the house of Israel**."
- **message**: "The **kingdom of heaven is at hand**."
- **works**: heal the sick, raise the dead, cleanse lepers, cast out demons
- **motive**: "**You received without paying, give without pay.**"
- **equipment**: no gold, silver or copper; **no bag**, no **two tunics**, no spare sandals — "the **labourer deserves his food**"
- **lodging**: find who is **worthy** and stay there; let your peace come upon the house
- **rejection**: "**shake off the dust from your feet**" — it will be more tolerable for **Sodom and Gomorrah** on the day of judgement
- **warning**: "I send you out as **sheep in the midst of wolves**; so be **wise as serpents and innocent as doves**."
They went out preaching repentance, cast out many demons and **anointed the sick with oil**.

## The Seventy (Luke 10)
The Lord appointed **seventy others** and sent them **two by two** ahead of Him into every town where He was about to come.
- "**The harvest is plentiful, but the labourers are few**; pray therefore the Lord of the harvest."
- "I send you out as **lambs in the midst of wolves**."
- carry **no purse, no bag, no sandals**; **salute no one on the road** (urgency)
- say, "**Peace be to this house**"; remain in the same house, **eating what is set before you**
- heal the sick and say, "The kingdom of God has come near to you."
- woes on unrepentant **Chorazin, Bethsaida and Capernaum**
- "**He who hears you hears me**, and he who rejects you rejects me."

## The return
The seventy returned **with joy**: "Lord, even the **demons are subject to us in your name**!" Jesus said, "I saw **Satan fall like lightning** from heaven," but added: "do not rejoice that the spirits are subject to you; **rejoice that your names are written in heaven**." He thanked the Father for revealing these things to **babes**.

## Lessons
mission is urgent; depend on God, not on wealth; work in partnership; serve without greed; expect rejection; the messenger represents Christ; salvation matters more than spectacular success. The limited mission to Israel was later widened to **all nations**.`,
