          notes: `## Bible references
**Mark 1:40–45; Matthew 8:5–13; Mark 2:1–12; 5:1–20; Luke 17:11–19**.

## The leper
A leper knelt before Jesus: "**If you will, you can make me clean.**" **Moved with pity**, Jesus **stretched out his hand and touched him**: "**I will; be clean.**" He was told to say nothing but to **show himself to the priest** and offer what **Moses commanded**. Instead he spread the news, so that Jesus could no longer openly enter a town.
*Note:* touching a leper broke a social barrier; Jesus respected the law.

## The centurion's servant
At **Capernaum** a **centurion** pleaded for his paralysed servant. When Jesus offered to come, he said, "Lord, **I am not worthy** to have you come under my roof; but **only say the word**, and my servant will be healed" — for he too was a man under authority. Jesus marvelled: "**Not even in Israel have I found such faith.**" Many will come **from east and west** and sit at table in the kingdom. The servant was healed **at that very moment**.
*Note:* a Gentile's faith; healing at a distance.

## The paralytic
The house in Capernaum was so crowded that **four men** removed the **roof** and let the paralytic down. Seeing **their faith**, Jesus said, "**My son, your sins are forgiven.**" The scribes thought, "It is **blasphemy**! Who can forgive sins but God alone?" Jesus asked which was easier — to say "your sins are forgiven" or "rise and walk" — and, "that you may know that **the Son of man has authority on earth to forgive sins**", told him to rise, take up his pallet and go home. All were amazed.

## The Gerasene demoniac
In the country of the **Gerasenes** a man with an unclean spirit lived **among the tombs**; chains could not hold him; he cried out and bruised himself with stones. He ran and worshipped Jesus; the spirit named itself "**Legion**; for we are many". The demons begged to enter a herd of about **two thousand swine**, which rushed into the sea and drowned. The people found the man **clothed and in his right mind** — and **begged Jesus to leave**. The man wished to go with Him, but was told, "**Go home to your friends, and tell them** how much the Lord has done for you." He proclaimed it in the **Decapolis**.

## The ten lepers
Between **Samaria and Galilee** ten lepers stood at a distance: "**Jesus, Master, have mercy on us.**" He said, "**Go and show yourselves to the priests.**" **As they went** they were cleansed. One, a **Samaritan**, turned back praising God and fell at Jesus' feet. "**Were not ten cleansed? Where are the nine?**" … "Rise and go your way; **your faith has made you well**."

## Lessons
faith, humility and persistence; the faith of friends helps others; Jesus forgives sins and frees from evil; people may value property above a person; **gratitude** is rare and precious; witness begins at home.`,
