          notes: `## Bible references
**Matthew 13:1–52; Mark 4:1–34**.

## What is a parable?
A story from everyday life used to teach a **spiritual truth**. Jesus used parables to make truth **memorable**, to provoke thought, to reveal the "**secrets of the kingdom**" to those willing to learn, while those with hardened hearts would "**see but not perceive**".

## The sower
Seed fell on four kinds of ground. **The seed is the word**.
- **the path** — birds ate it: those who hear without understanding; the **evil one snatches** the word away
- **rocky ground** — sprang up quickly, scorched for lack of root: those who receive with joy but **fall away when tribulation or persecution** comes
- **thorns** — choked: the **cares of the world and the delight in riches** make the word unfruitful
- **good soil** — yields **a hundredfold, sixty, thirty**: those who hear, understand and bear fruit
*Lesson:* the result depends on the hearer's heart; preachers should sow regardless.

## The weeds among the wheat
A man sowed good seed; while men slept **his enemy sowed weeds**. The servants offered to pull them up; the master said, "**Let both grow together until the harvest.**"
Interpretation: sower = the **Son of man**; field = the **world**; good seed = sons of the kingdom; weeds = sons of the evil one; enemy = the **devil**; harvest = the **close of the age**; reapers = **angels**. Evildoers will be thrown into the furnace of fire; the righteous will **shine like the sun**.
*Lesson:* good and evil coexist now; final judgement belongs to God.

## The mustard seed
The **smallest of seeds** becomes the greatest of shrubs, a tree where birds nest. *Lesson:* the kingdom's small beginning will have a great end.

## The leaven
A woman hid leaven in **three measures of meal** till all was leavened. *Lesson:* the kingdom works quietly from within and transforms the whole.

## The hidden treasure and the pearl
A man finds treasure in a field and **in his joy sells all** to buy the field; a merchant finds **one pearl of great value** and sells all. *Lesson:* the kingdom is worth every sacrifice.

## The net
A net gathers fish of every kind; the good are kept, the bad thrown away. So at the close of the age angels will **separate the evil from the righteous**.

## The householder
A scribe trained for the kingdom brings out of his treasure **what is new and what is old**.

## Application
examine how you hear God's word; be patient with an imperfect church; do not despise small beginnings; value the kingdom above all.`,
