          notes: `## Bible references
**John 6:25–40; 8:12; 9:5; 10:1–18; 11:17–27; 14:1–7; 15:1–11**.

## Background
In John's Gospel Jesus describes Himself in seven "**I am**" sayings. "I AM" echoes God's name revealed to Moses, so the sayings are claims about His **divine identity** and about what He gives to believers.

## 1. The bread of life (6:35)
After the feeding of the five thousand, the crowd sought Him for more bread and recalled the **manna**. Jesus said, "Do not labour for the **food which perishes** … **I am the bread of life**; he who comes to me shall not hunger, and he who believes in me shall never thirst." *Meaning:* He satisfies the deepest spiritual need and gives eternal life.

## 2. The light of the world (8:12; 9:5)
"**I am the light of the world**; he who follows me will not walk in darkness, but will have the light of life." The saying is illustrated by the healing of the **man born blind**. *Meaning:* He reveals God and guides out of sin and ignorance.

## 3. The door of the sheep (10:7–9)
"**I am the door**; if any one enters by me, he will be saved, and will go in and out and find pasture." *Meaning:* He is the only entrance to salvation and security. The **thief** comes to steal, kill and destroy; "I came that they may have **life, and have it abundantly**."

## 4. The good shepherd (10:11–18)
"**I am the good shepherd.** The good shepherd **lays down his life for the sheep**." The **hireling** flees when the wolf comes because he cares nothing for the sheep. "I **know my own and my own know me**." He has "**other sheep**, not of this fold" — "one flock, one shepherd". He lays down His life **of His own accord**. *Meaning:* sacrificial, personal care; a model for leaders.

## 5. The resurrection and the life (11:25–26)
To **Martha** at Bethany, when Lazarus had been dead **four days**: "**I am the resurrection and the life**; he who believes in me, though he die, yet shall he live." Martha confessed, "I believe that you are the Christ, the Son of God." *Meaning:* He has power over death, now and at the last day.

## 6. The way, the truth and the life (14:6)
"Let not your hearts be troubled … In my Father's house are **many rooms**; I go to **prepare a place** for you." **Thomas** said, "We do not know where you are going; how can we know the way?" — "**I am the way, and the truth, and the life; no one comes to the Father, but by me.**" To Philip: "He who has seen me has seen the Father."

## 7. The true vine (15:1–11)
"**I am the true vine, and my Father is the vinedresser.**" Fruitless branches are **taken away**; fruitful ones are **pruned**. "**Abide in me** … apart from me you can do **nothing**." Abiding means keeping His commandments; the result is much fruit, answered prayer and full joy.

## Lessons
depend on Christ daily; follow His light; leaders should serve sacrificially; face death with hope; stay united with Christ and bear fruit.`,
