          notes: `## Bible references
**John 3:16–18; 13:1–17, 34–35; 15:9–17; 1 John 3:16–18; 4:7–21**.

## God's love for the world
"**For God so loved the world that he gave his only Son**, that whoever believes in him should not perish but have **eternal life**." God sent the Son **not to condemn** the world but to save it. Love is thus the motive of salvation; it is **universal** ("the world"), **sacrificial** ("gave") and requires a response ("whoever believes"). The words were spoken in the conversation with **Nicodemus**, who was told he must be **born anew**.

## Love shown in service
Before the Passover, Jesus, "having loved his own … **loved them to the end**". He rose from supper, girded Himself with a **towel** and **washed the disciples' feet**. **Peter** objected; Jesus said, "If I do not wash you, you have no part in me." Afterwards: "If I then, your **Lord and Teacher**, have washed your feet, **you also ought to wash one another's feet**. I have given you an **example**."

## The new commandment
"**A new commandment I give to you, that you love one another; even as I have loved you.** By this all men will know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another."
- *new* because the standard is "**as I have loved you**"
- it is the **badge** of discipleship

## The greatest love
"**Greater love has no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.** You are my **friends** if you do what I command you. No longer do I call you servants … **You did not choose me, but I chose you** and appointed you that you should go and **bear fruit**."

## Love in 1 John
- "Beloved, let us love one another; for **love is of God** … **God is love**."
- "In this is love, **not that we loved God but that he loved us** and sent his Son to be the expiation for our sins."
- "**We love, because he first loved us.**"
- "If any one says, 'I love God,' and **hates his brother, he is a liar**; for he who does not love his brother whom he has seen, cannot love God whom he has not seen."
- "**Perfect love casts out fear.**"
- "If any one has the world's goods and sees his brother in need, yet closes his heart … let us not love **in word or speech but in deed and in truth**."

## Characteristics of Christian love
sacrificial, practical, humble, forgiving, impartial, obedient to Christ's commands.

## Application
care for the needy, the sick and strangers; reject tribalism, hatred and revenge; serve without seeking position; forgive; let love mark relationships at home, school and church.`,
